@page "/canadian-servers"
@layout PublicLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Canadian Data Sovereignty &amp; Security - Email Money App</PageTitle>

<section class="brochure-information-page">
    <h2>Canadian Data Sovereignty &amp; Security</h2>
    <p>
        At EMA, protecting donor data is a foundational priority. We ensure that all sensitive
        information remains strictly within Canadian borders, safeguarded by enterprise-grade
        infrastructure and stringent privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h3>Uncompromising Data Sovereignty</h3>
    <p>
        By keeping the platform’s hosted data exclusively in Canada, we protect donor
        information from foreign jurisdiction and international data access laws (such as the US
        CLOUD Act). Your data is governed solely by Canadian privacy legislation, ensuring
        complete data sovereignty and peace of mind for both you and your donors.
    </p>

    <h3>Secure Microsoft Azure Infrastructure</h3>
    <p>
        Our platform is built on Microsoft Azure's Canadian data centers (located in Toronto and
        Quebec City). This guarantees high availability, localized disaster recovery, and
        continuous 24/7 threat monitoring. Microsoft's infrastructure undergoes rigorous third-party
        audits (including ISO 27001 and SOC 2 Type 2), ensuring both physical and
        network security at every level.
    </p>

    <h3>End-to-End Encryption</h3>
    <p>
        Donor data is never left vulnerable. We employ robust encryption protocols to protect
        data both in transit (as it moves between the platform and users) and at rest (when it is
        safely stored in our databases), ensuring unauthorized parties cannot access sensitive
        information.
    </p>

    <h3>Compliance and Auditability</h3>
    <p>
        Our localized infrastructure directly supports EMA's operational audit requirements and
        regulatory objectives. We align with the Personal Information Protection and Electronic
        Documents Act (PIPEDA) and substantially similar provincial privacy laws, helping you
        meet the highest standards of accountability, data management, and donor trust.
    </p>

    <h3>Industry Resources on Canadian Data Security</h3>
    <p>
        For deeper insight into the regulatory and technical frameworks that guide our security
        architecture, explore the following resources:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada: PIPEDA Requirements in Brief</li>
        <li>Microsoft Trust Center: Azure Compliance Offerings for Canadian Privacy Laws</li>
    </ul>
</section>
